1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,380
假如有一种人工智能可以阅读神经网络的大脑
What if an AI could read a neural network's brain,

2
00:00:03,380 --> 00:00:06,560
然后完全不经过训练就重新编写它，会怎样？
and then rewrite it, without any training at all?

3
00:00:06,560 --> 00:00:11,562
MIT的研究人员刚发表了一项名为"权重空间编程"的研究。
Researchers at MIT just published something they call Weight-Space Programming.

4
00:00:11,562 --> 00:00:14,200
通常，要改变神经网络
Normally, to change a neural network,

5
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:16,722
你使用梯度下降来训练它
you train it with gradient descent.

6
00:00:16,722 --> 00:00:19,110
但这些研究人员跳过了这一步
These researchers skipped that.

7
00:00:19,110 --> 00:00:21,470
他们给了一款前沿的人工智能
They gave a frontier AI

8
00:00:21,470 --> 00:00:23,550
网络中的原始数字
the raw numbers inside a network,

9
00:00:23,550 --> 00:00:26,000
只是问了它几个问题
and just asked it questions.

10
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:30,670
首先是阅读。给它大约一万七千个原始权重
First, reading. Handed about seventeen thousand raw weights,

11
00:00:30,670 --> 00:00:33,770
人工智能正确地辨别出了网络训练的游戏是哪一种
the AI correctly named which game the network was trained on.

12
00:00:33,770 --> 00:00:37,890
《Breakout》《Pong》《Pac-Man》《Freeway》
Breakout, Pong, Pac-Man, Freeway.

13
00:00:37,890 --> 00:00:40,410
全都猜对了
All four, right.

14
00:00:40,410 --> 00:00:43,260
然后是写作。完全没有训练
Then, writing. With no training,

15
00:00:43,260 --> 00:00:45,840
没有数据，也没有试运行
no data, and no practice runs,

16
00:00:45,840 --> 00:00:49,760
它从零编写了一个能玩《Breakout》的网络。
it wrote a network from scratch that plays Breakout.

17
00:00:49,760 --> 00:00:54,692
它还打败了一个经过上亿步训练的网络
It beat a network trained for a hundred million steps.

18
00:00:54,692 --> 00:00:56,720
最疯狂的是：
And the wildest part:

19
00:00:56,720 --> 00:01:01,917
他们给了一款容易陷入思维循环的小型语言模型
they gave it a small language model that kept getting stuck in thinking loops.

20
00:01:01,917 --> 00:01:07,680
但人工智能在其权重内找到了问题所在
The AI found the problem inside the weights

21
00:01:07,680 --> 00:01:09,245
并对它们进行了仅仅百分之零点一六的编辑
and edited just point-zero-one-six percent of them.

22
00:01:09,245 --> 00:01:13,300
数学准确性从百分之八提高到了百分之四十八
Math accuracy jumped from eight percent to forty-eight percent.

23
00:01:15,680 --> 00:01:18,410
现在还言之过早。
It's early.

24
00:01:18,410 --> 00:01:22,270
在另一个没有循环问题的模型中
On another model that had no loop problem,

25
00:01:22,270 --> 00:01:24,370
AI 什么都改进不了
the AI couldn't improve anything.

26
00:01:24,370 --> 00:01:27,130
调整权重可以去除障碍
Editing weights can remove an obstacle,

27
00:01:27,130 --> 00:01:28,940
却不能增加一项能力
but it can't add an ability

28
00:01:28,940 --> 00:01:30,730
也就是模型所缺乏的能力。
the model lacks.

29
00:01:33,430 --> 00:01:38,080
但想象一下，仅通过阅读权重就能审计AI是否有隐藏后门。
But imagine auditing an AI for hidden backdoors

30
00:01:38,080 --> 00:01:40,467
仅仅通过读取它的权重。
just by reading its weights.

31
00:01:40,467 --> 00:01:45,940
我们或许正在见证一种全新编程AI方式的开始。
We may be watching the beginning of a new way to program AI.

32
00:01:45,940 --> 00:01:49,980
关注我了解更多，并在评论区告诉我：
Follow me for more, and tell me in the comments:

33
00:01:49,980 --> 00:01:53,440
你会信任AI去编辑另一个AI吗？
would you trust an AI to edit another AI?
